`PatternClipboard` holds the whole Pattern plus the Bank and slot it came from,
and answers two questions the screen would otherwise decide for itself:
`markedSlot(inBank:)` (the origin mark is drawn only in its own Bank, FR12) and
`destination(selected:armed:isRunning:)` (stopped the selected slot, running the
armed one if there is one and otherwise what sounds, FR8).

`TransportModel` stores it as an optional that starts empty, with `canPaste` and
`copiedSlotIndex` on top. It is memory only — no `Persistence`, no disk format,
no `schemaVersion` (FR3, NFR5).

